IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lsl-dates`

-- Long Service Leave Act 2018 (Vic) -- the rules.
--
-- Part 1 (s 5, and the s 3 definitions the rules use), Part 2 (entitlement, one employer, continuous employment, the
-- periods that count, ordinary pay and the s 16 normal weekly hours formulas, taking and paying leave, payment on
-- termination and on death, contracting out), Part 3 Division 1 (recovery, interest, the remedies for adverse action) and
-- the Division 3 duties a person meets (payments in lieu, working on leave, adverse action, records), Parts 4 to 6
-- (superior and accrued entitlements, disclosure). The employee's questions are in lsl-seat.l4, which imports this module
-- and never restates a rule.
--
-- Answers follow the rulings on negatives (NOTES.md): JUST FALSE where the text itself says no, NOTHING (with a
-- NOTHING-kind tag) where it does not answer. Judgments given to the Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court or to the
-- employer ("reasonable business grounds", "in the opinion of", "is satisfied", "cannot reasonably be held responsible")
-- are facts given to the rules, never guessed.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Long Service
-- Leave Act 2018, Version No. 006 (12 December 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with
-- the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Long Service Leave Act 2018`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a `and` b MEANS IF a LESS THAN b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` a `and` b MEANS IF a GREATER THAN b THEN a ELSE b

-- Nothing below zero.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not below zero` a MEANS `the greater of` a `and` 0

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`yes or no` b MEANS IF b THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The greater of two figures either of which may be missing (NOTHING where neither is there).
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE NUMBER, b IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the greater figure of` a `and` b MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN b
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
        WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (`the greater of` x `and` y)

§§ `Part 1 -- to whom the Act applies (ss 3, 5)`

-- s 5 "This Act does not apply in relation to an employee who -- (a) is entitled to long service leave under a Victorian
-- Act other than this Act, to the extent of any inconsistency with that other Victorian Act; or (b) is entitled to long
-- service leave under an employment agreement ..., to the extent of any inconsistency with that employment agreement if,
-- in the opinion of the Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court, the long service leave entitlements are more
-- favourable under that agreement than those provided by this Act; or (c) is employed by an employer who was exempted from
-- complying with Division 6 of Part 5 of the Long Service Leave Act 1992 under section 65 of that Act; or (d) is employed
-- under Part 2.3, 2.4 or 2A.1 of the Education and Training Reform Act 2006; or (e) is entitled under the Construction
-- Industry Long Service Leave Act 1997 to long service leave and to be paid benefits out of the fund ...".
-- s 3(1) "employee includes -- (a) a person employed by an employer to do any work for hire or reward and includes ... an
-- apprentice ... a casual or seasonal employee; and (b)-(f) [public sector employees, directors of public entities,
-- police officers and police reservists]". An open definition: outside its heads the Act does not answer.
DECLARE `How the Act applies to me` IS ONE OF
    `the Act applies to me`
    `the Act applies to me, except where it is inconsistent with the other Victorian Act or the more favourable agreement (s 5(a), (b))`
    `the Act does not apply to me (s 5(c), (d) or (e))`

GIVEN `I am an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another Victorian Act gives me long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers my agreement more favourable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my employer was exempted under the 1992 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am employed under the Education and Training Reform Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the construction industry scheme covers me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `How the Act applies to me`
`s 5 -- how the Act applies` `I am an employee` `another Victorian Act gives me long service leave` `the court considers my agreement more favourable` `my employer was exempted under the 1992 Act` `I am employed under the Education and Training Reform Act` `the construction industry scheme covers me` MEANS
    IF NOT `I am an employee`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (open definition: s 3(1) "employee includes"; outside its heads the Act does not answer)
    ELSE IF `my employer was exempted under the 1992 Act` OR `I am employed under the Education and Training Reform Act` OR `the construction industry scheme covers me`
         THEN JUST `the Act does not apply to me (s 5(c), (d) or (e))`
         ELSE IF `another Victorian Act gives me long service leave` OR `the court considers my agreement more favourable`
              THEN JUST `the Act applies to me, except where it is inconsistent with the other Victorian Act or the more favourable agreement (s 5(a), (b))`
              ELSE JUST `the Act applies to me`

§§ `Part 2 -- one employer (s 11)`

-- s 11 sets out "several situations in which an employee is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to have been employed by
-- one employer despite having been employed during the relevant period by more than one employer in a strict legal
-- sense". The answer is the day from which the employee's employment with the one employer is counted.
DECLARE `Why earlier employment might count` IS ONE OF
    `there is no earlier employer or business`
    `my earlier employer was a related body corporate, or had substantially the same directors or management (s 11(2))`
    `the business changed owner and my employment continued (s 11(3))`
    `the old owner dismissed me and the new owner re-employed me on the same or substantially the same work (s 11(5))`
    `the assets I worked with were transferred and the new owner continued my employment (s 11(6))`
    `I was dismissed, the assets I worked with were transferred, and the new employer employed me to work with them or similar assets (s 11(7), (8))`
    `my work was contracted out and I moved to the contractor as a consequence (s 11(9), (10))`

-- s 11(5) "is re-employed within 12 weeks after the day of the dismissal"; s 11(7)(d) "within 12 weeks after the day of
-- the dismissal". Re-employment on the day 12 weeks after the dismissal is in time (fork F2).
GIVEN `the day of re-employment` IS A DATE, `weeks` IS A NUMBER, `the day of the dismissal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `re-employed` `the day of re-employment` `within` `weeks` `weeks after` `the day of the dismissal` IF
    `the day` `the day of re-employment` `is on or before` (`the date` `weeks` `weeks after` `the day of the dismissal`)

GIVEN `the situation` IS A `Why earlier employment might count`
      `the day I first started` IS A DATE
      `the day I started with my present employer` IS A DATE
      `the day I was dismissed` IS A DATE
      `the day I was re-employed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 11 -- the day my employment with the one employer is counted from` `the situation` `the day I first started` `the day I started with my present employer` `the day I was dismissed` `the day I was re-employed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the situation`
    WHEN `there is no earlier employer or business` THEN `the day I started with my present employer`
    WHEN `the old owner dismissed me and the new owner re-employed me on the same or substantially the same work (s 11(5))` THEN
        IF `re-employed` `the day I was re-employed` `within` 12 `weeks after` `the day I was dismissed`
        THEN `the day I first started`
        ELSE `the day I started with my present employer`
    WHEN `I was dismissed, the assets I worked with were transferred, and the new employer employed me to work with them or similar assets (s 11(7), (8))` THEN
        IF `re-employed` `the day I was re-employed` `within` 12 `weeks after` `the day I was dismissed`
        THEN `the day I first started`
        ELSE `the day I started with my present employer`
    OTHERWISE `the day I first started`

§§ `Part 2 -- continuous employment (s 12)`

DECLARE `Kind of absence` IS ONE OF
    `annual leave`
    `long service leave`
    `parental leave`
    `carer's leave`
    `leave on account of illness or injury`
    `other leave my employment agreement provides for`
    `a gap between engagements as a casual or seasonal employee`
    `my employer ended or interrupted my employment to avoid long service leave`
    `the transfer of assets I usually work with to another employer`
    `my employment was terminated by my employer or by me, and I was re-employed`
    `my fixed-term contract expired, and I was re-employed`
    `my apprenticeship was completed, and I was re-employed`
    `a stand-down during industrial action`
    `a stand-down because of a breakdown of machinery or equipment`
    `a stand-down because of a stoppage of work`
    `an interruption arising from an industrial dispute`
    `another absence`

-- s 12(3) "A casual or seasonal employee's employment is taken to be continuous despite an absence from work that is
-- longer than 12 weeks ... if -- (a) the casual or seasonal employee and the employer so agree before the start of the
-- absence; or (b) the absence is due to the terms of engagement ...; or (c) the absence is caused by seasonal factors; or
-- (d) the employee has been employed by the employer on a regular and systematic basis and the employee has a reasonable
-- expectation of being re-engaged by the employer."
DECLARE `Why the gap between engagements` IS ONE OF
    `my employer and I agreed before it started that it would not break my employment`
    `it was due to the terms of my engagement`
    `it was caused by seasonal factors`
    `I had been employed on a regular and systematic basis and reasonably expected to be re-engaged`
    `none of these reasons`

-- s 12(2) leave; (3) casual gaps; (4) avoidance; (5) transfer of assets; (6) re-employment within 12 or 52 weeks; (7)
-- stand-downs; (8) industrial disputes. Each paragraph says when the employment "is taken to be continuous despite" an
-- absence. Where its "if" fails (re-employed too late, could have been usefully employed, the employer is responsible),
-- JUST FALSE for that paragraph. Where no paragraph speaks of the absence, NOTHING: the Act does not say what breaks
-- continuity.
GIVEN `the absence` IS A `Kind of absence`
      `I am casual or seasonal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `weeks of the absence` IS A NUMBER
      `why the gap` IS A `Why the gap between engagements`
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE
      `the day I was re-employed` IS A DATE
      `I could not be usefully employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer cannot reasonably be held responsible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12 -- my employment is continuous despite the absence` `the absence` `I am casual or seasonal` `weeks of the absence` `why the gap` `the day my employment ended` `the day I was re-employed` `I could not be usefully employed` `the employer cannot reasonably be held responsible` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the absence`
    WHEN `annual leave` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `long service leave` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- s 12(2)(c) "paid or unpaid parental leave (other than in the case of a casual or seasonal employee)"; (d) "in the
    -- case of a casual or seasonal employee, paid or unpaid parental leave that is not longer than 104 weeks". Longer than
    -- 104 weeks for a casual: JUST FALSE (fork F4).
    WHEN `parental leave` THEN
        IF `I am casual or seasonal`
        THEN `yes or no` (`weeks of the absence` AT MOST 104)
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `carer's leave` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `leave on account of illness or injury` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `other leave my employment agreement provides for` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- s 12(3) speaks only of gaps "longer than 12 weeks". A casual's gap of 12 weeks or less is read as an ending and a
    -- re-employment within 12 weeks under s 12(6)(a) (fork F5). A gap reached by neither: not a casual: NOTHING.
    WHEN `a gap between engagements as a casual or seasonal employee` THEN
        IF NOT `I am casual or seasonal`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 12(3) speaks only of a casual or seasonal employee)
        ELSE IF `weeks of the absence` AT MOST 12
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE CONSIDER `why the gap`
                  WHEN `none of these reasons` THEN JUST FALSE
                  OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `my employer ended or interrupted my employment to avoid long service leave` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the transfer of assets I usually work with to another employer` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `my employment was terminated by my employer or by me, and I was re-employed` THEN
        `yes or no` (`re-employed` `the day I was re-employed` `within` 12 `weeks after` `the day my employment ended`)
    WHEN `my fixed-term contract expired, and I was re-employed` THEN
        `yes or no` (`re-employed` `the day I was re-employed` `within` 12 `weeks after` `the day my employment ended`)
    WHEN `my apprenticeship was completed, and I was re-employed` THEN
        `yes or no` (`re-employed` `the day I was re-employed` `within` 52 `weeks after` `the day my employment ended`)
    WHEN `a stand-down during industrial action` THEN `yes or no` `I could not be usefully employed`
    WHEN `a stand-down because of a breakdown of machinery or equipment` THEN
        `yes or no` (`I could not be usefully employed` AND `the employer cannot reasonably be held responsible`)
    WHEN `a stand-down because of a stoppage of work` THEN
        `yes or no` (`I could not be usefully employed` AND `the employer cannot reasonably be held responsible`)
    WHEN `an interruption arising from an industrial dispute` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another absence` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 12 lists the absences that keep employment continuous and says nothing of others)

-- s 12(9) "industrial action means any of the following kinds of action -- (a) [work performed differently, restricting
-- or delaying it]; (b) a ban, limitation or restriction on the performance of work ...; (c) a failure or refusal by
-- employees to attend for work or ... to perform any work at all ...; (d) an employer prevents an employee from performing
-- work ... without terminating that contract." (10) "Despite anything to the contrary in subsection (9), industrial action
-- does not include -- (a) action by employees that is authorised or agreed to by the employer ...; (b) action by an
-- employer that is authorised or agreed to by, or on behalf of, employees ...; (c) action by an employee if -- (i) the
-- action was based on a reasonable concern of the employee about an imminent risk to the employee's health or safety; and
-- (ii) the employee did not unreasonably fail to comply with a direction of the employer to perform other available work
-- ... that was safe and appropriate". A "means" definition: outside it, JUST FALSE.
DECLARE `Kind of action` IS ONE OF
    `employees performing work differently so that it is restricted, limited or delayed`
    `a ban, limitation or restriction on performing, accepting or offering for work`
    `employees failing or refusing to attend for work or to perform any work`
    `an employer preventing employees from working without terminating their contracts`
    `none of these kinds of action`

GIVEN `the action` IS A `Kind of action`
      `the other side authorised or agreed to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was based on a reasonable concern about an imminent risk to health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee did not unreasonably refuse other safe and appropriate work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(9), (10) -- it is industrial action` `the action` `the other side authorised or agreed to it` `it was based on a reasonable concern about an imminent risk to health or safety` `the employee did not unreasonably refuse other safe and appropriate work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the action`
    WHEN `none of these kinds of action` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the other side authorised or agreed to it`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF `it was based on a reasonable concern about an imminent risk to health or safety` AND `the employee did not unreasonably refuse other safe and appropriate work`
             THEN CONSIDER `the action`
                  WHEN `an employer preventing employees from working without terminating their contracts` THEN JUST TRUE
                  OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
             ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 2 -- the periods that count (ss 13, 14)`

-- s 13(1) "The following periods of absence from work referred to in section 12 are taken to be periods of employment ...
-- (a) a period of paid leave; (b) if a period of unpaid leave is less than or is 52 weeks, that period; (c) if a period of
-- unpaid leave is more than 52 weeks, the initial 52 weeks; (d) if a period of unpaid leave is more than 52 weeks, the
-- entire period of unpaid leave if -- (i) the period of absence is taken to be a period of employment in accordance with
-- the relevant employment agreement; or (ii) the employer and the employee agreed in writing before the leave was taken
-- that the period is taken to be a period of employment; or (iii) the leave is taken on account of illness or injury or is
-- any other form of leave provided for under the relevant employment agreement; (e) a period of absence arising from --
-- (i) an interruption to, or termination of, employment caused by the employer with the intention of avoiding an
-- obligation in relation to long service leave; or (ii) the transfer of assets ...".
-- s 14 "... are not taken to be periods of employment ... (a) a period of unpaid leave in excess of 52 weeks (other than the
-- initial 52 weeks) unless [the same three]; (b) an absence following the ending of the employee's employment described in
-- section 12(6)(a) or (b); (c) an absence caused by an employer standing down the employee described in section 12(7)(a),
-- (b) or (c); (d) an interruption described in section 12(8)."
-- The answer is the number of weeks of the absence that count. Absences neither section speaks of: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the absence` IS A `Kind of absence`
      `it was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `weeks of the absence` IS A NUMBER
      `my employment agreement counts it as employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `we agreed in writing before the leave that it counts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`ss 13, 14 -- the weeks of the absence that count` `the absence` `it was paid` `weeks of the absence` `my employment agreement counts it as employment` `we agreed in writing before the leave that it counts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the absence`
    WHEN `annual leave` THEN `leave that counts`
    WHEN `long service leave` THEN `leave that counts`
    WHEN `parental leave` THEN `leave that counts`
    WHEN `carer's leave` THEN `leave that counts`
    WHEN `leave on account of illness or injury` THEN JUST `weeks of the absence`
    WHEN `other leave my employment agreement provides for` THEN JUST `weeks of the absence`
    WHEN `a gap between engagements as a casual or seasonal employee` THEN
        IF `weeks of the absence` AT MOST 12
        THEN JUST 0
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: neither s 13 nor s 14 speaks of a s 12(3) gap; fork F5)
    WHEN `my employer ended or interrupted my employment to avoid long service leave` THEN JUST `weeks of the absence`
    WHEN `the transfer of assets I usually work with to another employer` THEN JUST `weeks of the absence`
    WHEN `my employment was terminated by my employer or by me, and I was re-employed` THEN JUST 0
    WHEN `my fixed-term contract expired, and I was re-employed` THEN JUST 0
    WHEN `my apprenticeship was completed, and I was re-employed` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 14(b) names only s 12(6)(a) and (b); s 13 does not name s 12(6)(c))
    WHEN `a stand-down during industrial action` THEN JUST 0
    WHEN `a stand-down because of a breakdown of machinery or equipment` THEN JUST 0
    WHEN `a stand-down because of a stoppage of work` THEN JUST 0
    WHEN `an interruption arising from an industrial dispute` THEN JUST 0
    WHEN `another absence` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: not an absence s 12 refers to)
    WHERE
        `leave that counts` MEANS
            IF `it was paid`
            THEN JUST `weeks of the absence`
            ELSE IF `weeks of the absence` AT MOST 52
                 THEN JUST `weeks of the absence`
                 ELSE IF `my employment agreement counts it as employment` OR `we agreed in writing before the leave that it counts`
                      THEN JUST `weeks of the absence`
                      ELSE JUST 52

-- s 13(2) "If an employee enters into a contract of employment with an employer within 52 weeks after completing an
-- apprenticeship with the employer, the period of apprenticeship is taken to be a period of employment ...". An "if".
GIVEN `the day my apprenticeship was completed` IS A DATE, `the day I entered the contract` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(2) -- my apprenticeship counts` `the day my apprenticeship was completed` `the day I entered the contract` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`re-employed` `the day I entered the contract` `within` 52 `weeks after` `the day my apprenticeship was completed`)

§§ `Part 2 -- entitlement (ss 6, 7)`

-- s 6 "At any time after completing 7 years of continuous employment with one employer, an employee is entitled to an
-- amount of long service leave on ordinary pay equal to 1/60th of the employee's total period of continuous employment
-- less any period of long service leave taken during that period."
--
-- The period runs from the day it is counted from (s 11) to the day asked about, both included, less the weeks of absence
-- that do not count (ss 13, 14). 7 years are completed when that period is at least as long as the 7 calendar years that
-- follow the day it is counted from (fork F3). The entitlement is 1/60th of the period, in weeks, less the weeks of long
-- service leave already taken (fork F6), never below zero.
GIVEN `the day it is counted from` IS A DATE, `the day asked about` IS A DATE, `weeks that do not count` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 6 -- the days of continuous employment` `the day it is counted from` `the day asked about` `weeks that do not count` MEANS
    (`the days from` `the day it is counted from` `to` `the day asked about` PLUS 1) MINUS (`weeks that do not count` TIMES 7)

GIVEN `the day it is counted from` IS A DATE, `the day asked about` IS A DATE, `weeks that do not count` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6 -- I have completed 7 years` `the day it is counted from` `the day asked about` `weeks that do not count` IF
    `s 6 -- the days of continuous employment` `the day it is counted from` `the day asked about` `weeks that do not count`
        AT LEAST `the days from` `the day it is counted from` `to` (`the same day` 7 `years after` `the day it is counted from`)

GIVEN `the day it is counted from` IS A DATE, `the day asked about` IS A DATE, `weeks that do not count` IS A NUMBER, `weeks already taken` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 6 -- the weeks of long service leave` `the day it is counted from` `the day asked about` `weeks that do not count` `weeks already taken` MEANS
    IF `s 6 -- I have completed 7 years` `the day it is counted from` `the day asked about` `weeks that do not count`
    THEN `not below zero` ((`the days` DIVIDED BY 7 DIVIDED BY 60) MINUS `weeks already taken`)
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the days` MEANS `s 6 -- the days of continuous employment` `the day it is counted from` `the day asked about` `weeks that do not count`

-- s 7 "Long service leave does not include any public holiday occurring, or annual leave taken, during the period when the
-- long service leave is taken." The weeks of long service leave a period of leave uses.
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE, `public holidays` IS A NUMBER, `days of annual leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 7 -- the weeks of long service leave the period uses` `the first day` `the last day` `public holidays` `days of annual leave` MEANS
    `not below zero` (((`the days from` `the first day` `to` `the last day` PLUS 1) MINUS `public holidays` MINUS `days of annual leave`) DIVIDED BY 7)

§§ `Part 2 -- leave in advance (s 8)`

-- s 8(3) "If an employee takes long service leave before the employee is entitled to the long service leave and the
-- employee's employment ends, the employer may deduct from any payment payable to the employee as a result of the ending of
-- the employment an amount equal to the amount paid to the employee for the leave (if any) in respect of which the
-- employee will not become entitled." The most that may be deducted: the pay for the weeks of advance leave beyond what
-- the employee had become entitled to when the employment ended (fork F7).
GIVEN `weeks of leave taken in advance` IS A NUMBER, `the amount paid for it` IS A NUMBER, `weeks I had become entitled to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 8(3) -- the most that may be deducted` `weeks of leave taken in advance` `the amount paid for it` `weeks I had become entitled to` MEANS
    IF `weeks of leave taken in advance` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the amount paid for it` TIMES (`the lesser of` (`not below zero` (`weeks of leave taken in advance` MINUS `weeks I had become entitled to`)) `and` `weeks of leave taken in advance`) DIVIDED BY `weeks of leave taken in advance`

§§ `Part 2 -- ordinary pay and normal weekly hours (ss 15, 16, 17)`

-- s 15(1) "ordinary pay -- (a) means the pay that an employee is entitled to receive on the day on which the employee starts
-- long service leave, calculated on the employee's normal weekly hours at the employee's ordinary time rate of pay; and (b)
-- includes the cash value of any board or lodging ...". (2) "If an ordinary time rate of pay is not fixed for an employee's
-- work under the relevant employment agreement, the employee's ordinary time rate of pay is the greatest of the following --
-- (a) the average weekly rate earned by the employee in the 52 weeks immediately before the employee starts long service
-- leave; (b) ... in the 260 weeks ...; (c) ... during the employee's period of continuous employment with the employer ...".
-- s 15(2)'s figures are weekly: they are taken as the weekly pay, not multiplied again by hours (fork F8, finding 1).
GIVEN `my rate is fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my normal weekly hours` IS A NUMBER
      `my hourly rate` IS A NUMBER
      `average weekly earnings over 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `average weekly earnings over 260 weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `average weekly earnings over the whole period` IS A NUMBER
      `weekly cash value of board or lodging` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 15 -- my weekly ordinary pay` `my rate is fixed` `my normal weekly hours` `my hourly rate` `average weekly earnings over 52 weeks` `average weekly earnings over 260 weeks` `average weekly earnings over the whole period` `weekly cash value of board or lodging` MEANS
    (IF `my rate is fixed`
     THEN `my normal weekly hours` TIMES `my hourly rate`
     ELSE `the greater of` (`the greater of` `average weekly earnings over 52 weeks` `and` `average weekly earnings over 260 weeks`) `and` `average weekly earnings over the whole period`)
    PLUS `weekly cash value of board or lodging`

-- s 16(2)(a), formula 18-12a006-F1 (the .formulas.md sidecar): A = (B + C) / (52 - D), where B is the hours worked during
-- the 52 weeks, C the hours of paid leave during them and D the weeks of unpaid leave during them. With no week left to
-- divide by, the formula gives nothing.
GIVEN `hours worked` IS A NUMBER, `hours of paid leave` IS A NUMBER, `weeks of unpaid leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 16(2)(a) -- the 52-week average` `hours worked` `hours of paid leave` `weeks of unpaid leave` MEANS
    IF (52 MINUS `weeks of unpaid leave`) GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST ((`hours worked` PLUS `hours of paid leave`) DIVIDED BY (52 MINUS `weeks of unpaid leave`))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: the formula divides by zero)

-- s 16(2)(b), formula 18-12a006-F2: A = (B + C) / (260 - D), over the 260 weeks.
GIVEN `hours worked` IS A NUMBER, `hours of paid leave` IS A NUMBER, `weeks of unpaid leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 16(2)(b) -- the 260-week average` `hours worked` `hours of paid leave` `weeks of unpaid leave` MEANS
    IF (260 MINUS `weeks of unpaid leave`) GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST ((`hours worked` PLUS `hours of paid leave`) DIVIDED BY (260 MINUS `weeks of unpaid leave`))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: the formula divides by zero)

-- s 16(2)(c), formula 18-12a006-F3: A = (B + C) / (D - E), over the last period of continuous employment, D its weeks and
-- E the weeks of unpaid leave in it.
GIVEN `hours worked` IS A NUMBER, `hours of paid leave` IS A NUMBER, `weeks of the period` IS A NUMBER, `weeks of unpaid leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 16(2)(c) -- the whole-period average` `hours worked` `hours of paid leave` `weeks of the period` `weeks of unpaid leave` MEANS
    IF (`weeks of the period` MINUS `weeks of unpaid leave`) GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST ((`hours worked` PLUS `hours of paid leave`) DIVIDED BY (`weeks of the period` MINUS `weeks of unpaid leave`))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: the formula divides by zero)

-- s 16(1) "This section applies if -- (a) no normal weekly number of hours of work is fixed ...; or (b) the normal weekly
-- number of hours of work is fixed but is changed one or more times during the 104 weeks immediately before the employee
-- starts long service leave." (2) "... is taken to be the greatest of the following". Where s 16 does not apply, the
-- fixed hours.
GIVEN `my hours are fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my fixed weekly hours` IS A NUMBER
      `my hours changed in the last 104 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `hours worked in 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `paid leave hours in 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `unpaid leave weeks in 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `hours worked in 260 weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `paid leave hours in 260 weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `unpaid leave weeks in 260 weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `hours worked in the whole period` IS A NUMBER
      `paid leave hours in the whole period` IS A NUMBER
      `weeks of the whole period` IS A NUMBER
      `unpaid leave weeks in the whole period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 16 -- my normal weekly hours` `my hours are fixed` `my fixed weekly hours` `my hours changed in the last 104 weeks` `hours worked in 52 weeks` `paid leave hours in 52 weeks` `unpaid leave weeks in 52 weeks` `hours worked in 260 weeks` `paid leave hours in 260 weeks` `unpaid leave weeks in 260 weeks` `hours worked in the whole period` `paid leave hours in the whole period` `weeks of the whole period` `unpaid leave weeks in the whole period` MEANS
    IF `my hours are fixed` AND (NOT `my hours changed in the last 104 weeks`)
    THEN JUST `my fixed weekly hours`
    ELSE `the greater figure of` (`the greater figure of` `the first` `and` `the second`) `and` `the third`
    WHERE
        `the first` MEANS `s 16(2)(a) -- the 52-week average` `hours worked in 52 weeks` `paid leave hours in 52 weeks` `unpaid leave weeks in 52 weeks`
        `the second` MEANS `s 16(2)(b) -- the 260-week average` `hours worked in 260 weeks` `paid leave hours in 260 weeks` `unpaid leave weeks in 260 weeks`
        `the third` MEANS `s 16(2)(c) -- the whole-period average` `hours worked in the whole period` `paid leave hours in the whole period` `weeks of the whole period` `unpaid leave weeks in the whole period`

-- s 17(1) "This section applies if an employee is -- (a) working in suitable employment (within the meaning of section 3 of
-- the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013); or (b) absent from work because of a workplace illness or
-- injury and is in receipt of any compensation in the form of weekly payments ...". (2) "An employee's normal weekly hours
-- and ordinary time rate of pay are to be taken to be the greater of the following -- (a) ... immediately before the
-- employee starts long service leave; (b) ... immediately before the employee developed the relevant illness or suffered
-- the relevant injury." The pair giving the greater weekly pay is taken (fork F9). The answer is the weekly pay (hours times
-- rate) on the pair taken.
GIVEN `s 17 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `hours before the leave` IS A NUMBER
      `rate before the leave` IS A NUMBER
      `hours before the injury` IS A NUMBER
      `rate before the injury` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 17 -- my weekly pay on the hours and rate taken` `s 17 applies` `hours before the leave` `rate before the leave` `hours before the injury` `rate before the injury` MEANS
    IF `s 17 applies`
    THEN `the greater of` (`hours before the leave` TIMES `rate before the leave`) `and` (`hours before the injury` TIMES `rate before the injury`)
    ELSE `hours before the leave` TIMES `rate before the leave`

§§ `Part 2 -- taking and being paid for leave (ss 18 to 22)`

-- s 18(1) "An employee may make a request to the employee's employer to take long service leave for a period of not less
-- than 1 day." (2) "An employer must grant an employee's request to take long service leave as soon as practicable after
-- receiving the request unless the employer has reasonable business grounds for refusing the request." s 3(1) "reasonable
-- business grounds includes [no capacity or impractical to change others' arrangements, significant loss of efficiency or
-- productivity, significant negative impact on customer service]". A request for less than 1 day is not a s 18(1) request
-- (JUST FALSE, fork F10); no leave to take: NOTHING (fork F10).
GIVEN `days requested` IS A NUMBER, `I have long service leave to take` IS A BOOLEAN, `the employer has reasonable business grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18 -- my employer must grant my request` `days requested` `I have long service leave to take` `the employer has reasonable business grounds` MEANS
    IF NOT `I have long service leave to take`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 18 speaks of a request to take long service leave the employee has)
    ELSE IF `days requested` LESS THAN 1
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE `yes or no` (NOT `the employer has reasonable business grounds`)

-- s 19(1) "An employer may direct an employee to take long service leave at a specified time and for a specified period by
-- giving the employee at least 12 weeks' written notice." (2) "Subject to an order of the Industrial Division of the
-- Magistrates' Court, an employee must comply with a direction given under subsection (1)." Notice given on a day, with the
-- leave starting on or after the day 12 weeks later, is at least 12 weeks' notice (fork F11).
GIVEN `the notice was written` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day notice was given` IS A DATE, `the day the leave starts` IS A DATE, `the court has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19 -- I must comply with the direction` `the notice was written` `the day notice was given` `the day the leave starts` `the court has ordered otherwise` MEANS
    `yes or no` (    `the notice was written`
                 AND `the day` (`the date` 12 `weeks after` `the day notice was given`) `is on or before` `the day the leave starts`
                 AND (NOT `the court has ordered otherwise`))

-- s 20(1) "An employer must give an employee the pay ... in any way and at any time that is agreed to by the employee and
-- the employer before the start of the long service leave." (2) "If no agreement exists, ... in one of the following ways --
-- (a) pay in full when the employee starts the long service leave; (b) pay at the same time and in the same manner as if the
-- employee were not taking long service leave."
DECLARE `How I must be paid on leave` IS ONE OF
    `in the way and at the time we agreed before the leave started (s 20(1))`
    `either in full when the leave starts, or at the same times and in the same way as if I were not on leave (s 20(2))`

GIVEN `we agreed before the leave started` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How I must be paid on leave`
`s 20 -- how I must be paid on leave` `we agreed before the leave started` MEANS
    IF `we agreed before the leave started`
    THEN `in the way and at the time we agreed before the leave started (s 20(1))`
    ELSE `either in full when the leave starts, or at the same times and in the same way as if I were not on leave (s 20(2))`

-- s 21(1) "If the ordinary pay of an employee who is on long service leave increases, the employee is entitled to be paid at
-- the increased rate from the time of the increase." (2) "If the employee was paid in full at the start ... or was paid in
-- advance ..., the employer must pay the additional amount resulting from the increase as soon as that period ends."
GIVEN `weekly pay before the increase` IS A NUMBER, `weekly pay after the increase` IS A NUMBER, `weeks of leave from the increase` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21 -- the extra pay for the increase` `weekly pay before the increase` `weekly pay after the increase` `weeks of leave from the increase` MEANS
    `not below zero` (`weekly pay after the increase` MINUS `weekly pay before the increase`) TIMES `weeks of leave from the increase`

-- s 22(1) "An employee may request ... a period of long service leave -- (a) twice as long as the period to which the
-- employee would otherwise be entitled; and (b) at a rate of pay equal to half the employee's ordinary pay." (2) "An
-- employer must grant a request made under subsection (1) unless the employer has reasonable business grounds for refusing
-- the request."
GIVEN `weeks of leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22 -- the weeks at half pay` `weeks of leave` MEANS `weeks of leave` TIMES 2

GIVEN `the employer has reasonable business grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22 -- my employer must grant half-pay leave` `the employer has reasonable business grounds` MEANS
    `yes or no` (NOT `the employer has reasonable business grounds`)

§§ `Part 2 -- the end of employment and death (ss 9, 10)`

-- s 9(1) "If an employee's employment ends (other than because of the employee's death) before the employee has taken all
-- the long service leave to which the employee is entitled -- (a) the employee is taken to have started long service leave
-- on the day on which the employment ends; and (b) the full amount of the employee's long service leave entitlement,
-- calculated as at the day on which the employment ends, is due and payable to the employee on that day." (2) "The employer
-- ... must pay the employee the full amount ...". s 10(1) "If an employee dies before taking all the long service leave to
-- which the employee is entitled, the employee's employer must pay to the employee's personal representative the full
-- amount of the long service leave entitlement still owed to the employee." The amount: the weeks of the s 6 entitlement as
-- at the last day (that day counted, fork F12) times the weekly ordinary pay (ss 15 to 17; for a death, s 10(3)).
GIVEN `the day it is counted from` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE, `weeks that do not count` IS A NUMBER, `weeks already taken` IS A NUMBER, `weekly ordinary pay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ss 9, 10 -- the full amount` `the day it is counted from` `the last day` `weeks that do not count` `weeks already taken` `weekly ordinary pay` MEANS
    `s 6 -- the weeks of long service leave` `the day it is counted from` `the last day` `weeks that do not count` `weeks already taken` TIMES `weekly ordinary pay`

-- The parties and acts of the rules with deadlines.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `my employer`, `me`
DECLARE `What is done` IS ONE OF
    `pay my long service leave` HAS `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `commence a proceeding to recover the money` HAS `after a written demand` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 9(2), (3): the employer MUST pay the full amount on the day the employment ends (day 0, WITHIN 0), LEST the offence
-- (12 penalty units a day for a natural person, 60 for a body corporate, "for each day during which the offence
-- continues"). A payment of less than the full amount does not count.
GIVEN `the amount owed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `What is done`
`s 9(2) -- pay the full amount on the day the employment ends` `the amount owed` MEANS
    PARTY `my employer`
    MUST `pay my long service leave` `the amount` PROVIDED `the amount` AT LEAST `the amount owed`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `my employer` BECAUSE "the full amount of long service leave was not paid on the day the employment ended (s 9(1)(b), (2)); the obligation continues until it is paid (s 9(3))"

-- s 26(4) "A proceeding under this section must be commenced within 6 years after the employee's entitlement to the money
-- arises." (5) "Before a proceeding may be commenced under this section, the employee or organisation ... must give the
-- employer a written demand for the money owed." The employee DOes commence, after a written demand, WITHIN the days to
-- the last day, LEST out of time. A proceeding without a demand does not count.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `What is done`
`s 26(4), (5) -- commence after a demand within 6 years` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `me`
    DO `commence a proceeding to recover the money` `demanded` PROVIDED `demanded`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `me` BECAUSE "no proceeding under s 26 was commenced, after a written demand, within 6 years after the entitlement to the money arose (s 26(4), (5))"

-- The helper that runs a rule over what happened (as in the County Court Act 1958 and Victims of Crime encodings). On the
-- stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never
-- exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `What is done`
      `the party` IS A `Party`
      `the act` IS A `What is done`
      `the day it was done` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `done in time under` `the rule` `by` `the party` `doing` `the act` `on day` `the day it was done` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day it was done`), (EVENT `the party` `the act` `the day it was done`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Whether my long service leave was paid on time` IS ONE OF
    `nothing is owed under s 9`
    `paid in full on or before the day my employment ended`
    `paid in full, but late: it was due on the day my employment ended (s 9(1)(b))`
    `not yet paid in full, and due today (s 9(1)(b))`
    `not yet paid in full, and overdue since the day my employment ended: the obligation continues until it is paid (s 9(3))`

GIVEN `the amount owed` IS A NUMBER
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE
      `I have been paid in full` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I was paid in full` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Whether my long service leave was paid on time`
`s 9 -- whether I was paid on time` `the amount owed` `the day my employment ended` `I have been paid in full` `the day I was paid in full` `today` MEANS
    IF `the amount owed` AT MOST 0
    THEN `nothing is owed under s 9`
    ELSE IF `I have been paid in full`
         THEN IF `done in time under` (`s 9(2) -- pay the full amount on the day the employment ends` `the amount owed`) `by` `my employer` `doing` (`pay my long service leave` `the amount owed`) `on day` (`not below zero` (`the days from` `the day my employment ended` `to` `the day I was paid in full`))
              THEN `paid in full on or before the day my employment ended`
              ELSE `paid in full, but late: it was due on the day my employment ended (s 9(1)(b))`
         ELSE IF `the day` `today` `is on or before` `the day my employment ended`
              THEN `not yet paid in full, and due today (s 9(1)(b))`
              ELSE `not yet paid in full, and overdue since the day my employment ended: the obligation continues until it is paid (s 9(3))`

§§ `Part 2 -- contracting out (s 23)`

-- s 23(1) "A provision in an employment agreement or a relevant deed that annuls, varies or excludes any provision of this
-- Act or of the Long Service Leave Act 1992 is of no effect ...". (2) "This section does not affect any provision ... to the
-- extent of any inconsistency with this Act if, in the opinion of the Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court, the
-- long service leave entitlements are more favourable under the agreement or the deed ...". (3) "relevant deed means a deed
-- or agreement between an employer and an employee ... executed at any time before, during or after the employment"; the
-- Note: "A deed of settlement between a former employer and a former employee is an example of a relevant deed."
-- The answer: whether the term can have effect. A term that does not annul, vary or exclude the Act: s 23 is silent.
GIVEN `the term annuls, varies or excludes the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court considers the agreement more favourable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23 -- the term can have effect` `the term annuls, varies or excludes the Act` `the court considers the agreement more favourable` MEANS
    IF NOT `the term annuls, varies or excludes the Act`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 23 speaks only of terms that annul, vary or exclude the Act)
    ELSE `yes or no` `the court considers the agreement more favourable`

§§ `Part 3 -- recovering money (ss 24, 26)`

-- s 26(4): the last day for commencing is the same day 6 years after the day the entitlement arose (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day the entitlement arose` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 26(4) -- the last day to commence` `the day the entitlement arose` MEANS `the same day` 6 `years after` `the day the entitlement arose`

GIVEN `the day the entitlement arose` IS A DATE, `the day I commence` IS A DATE, `I gave a written demand first` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26 -- my proceeding is in time` `the day the entitlement arose` `the day I commence` `I gave a written demand first` MEANS
    IF `the day` `the day I commence` `is before` `the day the entitlement arose`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: no money is owed yet, so s 26(4) has not begun to run)
    ELSE `yes or no` (`done in time under` (`s 26(4), (5) -- commence after a demand within 6 years` (`the days from` `the day the entitlement arose` `to` (`s 26(4) -- the last day to commence` `the day the entitlement arose`))) `by` `me` `doing` (`commence a proceeding to recover the money` `I gave a written demand first`) `on day` (`the days from` `the day the entitlement arose` `to` `the day I commence`))

-- s 26(6) "The Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court may order an employer to pay interest ... if it is satisfied
-- that the employer -- (a) had reasonable notice of the employee's claim; and (b) had no reasonable grounds on which to
-- dispute the claim; and (c) in the circumstances should have paid the claim without the need for a proceeding ...". (7)
-- "The interest must not be greater than the rate fixed under section 2 of the Penalty Interest Rates Act 1983 ...".
GIVEN `reasonable notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `no reasonable grounds to dispute` IS A BOOLEAN, `should have paid without a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(6) -- interest may be ordered` `reasonable notice` `no reasonable grounds to dispute` `should have paid without a proceeding` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`reasonable notice` AND `no reasonable grounds to dispute` AND `should have paid without a proceeding`)

§§ `Part 3 -- adverse action and its remedies (ss 27, 36)`

-- s 36(6) "an employer takes adverse action against an employee if the employer -- (a) dismisses the employee; or (b)
-- injures the employee in the employee's employment; or (c) alters the position of the employee to the employee's
-- prejudice; or (d) discriminates between the employee and other employees of the employer; or (e) knowingly or recklessly
-- makes a false representation about the employee's long service leave entitlements."
DECLARE `What my employer did` IS ONE OF
    `dismissed me`
    `injured me in my employment`
    `altered my position to my prejudice`
    `discriminated between me and other employees`
    `knowingly or recklessly misrepresented my long service leave entitlements`
    `none of these things`

-- s 36(1) to (4): "because the employee is entitled to long service leave or any other entitlement under this Act"; "seeks
-- to exercise"; "makes an enquiry as to"; "applies to the Industrial Division ... for an order in relation to a direction to
-- take long service leave under section 19(1)".
DECLARE `The reason I say it was done` IS ONE OF
    `because I am entitled to long service leave or another entitlement under the Act`
    `because I sought to exercise my entitlement`
    `because I enquired about my entitlement`
    `because I applied to the court about a direction to take leave`
    `no such reason`

-- s 36(5) "the onus of proving that the adverse action by the employer was not actuated by any reason referred to in
-- subsection (1), (2), (3) or (4) ... lies on the employer." No adverse action, or the employer proves the reason was not
-- one of those: JUST FALSE ("if"; "because"). No reason alleged: NOTHING.
GIVEN `what was done` IS A `What my employer did`, `the reason` IS A `The reason I say it was done`, `my employer proves it was not for that reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36 -- my employer took adverse action against me` `what was done` `the reason` `my employer proves it was not for that reason` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what was done`
    WHEN `none of these things` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the reason`
        WHEN `no such reason` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 36 reaches only action taken for the reasons it names)
        OTHERWISE `yes or no` (NOT `my employer proves it was not for that reason`)

-- s 27(2) "If the adverse action ... was the dismissal of the employee and the Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court
-- considers that it would be impracticable to reinstate the employee, the Court may order the employer to pay the employee
-- an amount of compensation not exceeding the amount of remuneration of the employee during the 52 weeks immediately before
-- the employee's dismissal."
GIVEN `the employer contravened s 36` IS A BOOLEAN, `it was my dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court considers reinstatement impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN, `remuneration in the 52 weeks before dismissal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 27(2) -- the most compensation` `the employer contravened s 36` `it was my dismissal` `the court considers reinstatement impracticable` `remuneration in the 52 weeks before dismissal` MEANS
    IF `the employer contravened s 36` AND `it was my dismissal` AND `the court considers reinstatement impracticable`
    THEN JUST `remuneration in the 52 weeks before dismissal`
    ELSE JUST 0

§§ `Part 3 -- payments in lieu, working on leave, records (ss 34, 35, 37)`

-- s 34(2) "An employee must not accept any payment in lieu of long service leave, or in lieu of any part of long service
-- leave, except as permitted under this or any other Act or under the relevant fair work instrument." Penalty: 12 penalty
-- units. The s 9 payment on the end of employment is permitted by this Act. Once the "except" is met, JUST TRUE (fork F13).
GIVEN `it is my payment when my employment ends` IS A BOOLEAN, `another Act or my fair work instrument permits it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34 -- I may accept a payment in lieu` `it is my payment when my employment ends` `another Act or my fair work instrument permits it` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`it is my payment when my employment ends` OR `another Act or my fair work instrument permits it`)

-- s 35(1) "An employee who is on long service leave must not work for hire or reward in relation to the hours during which
-- the employee is taking long service leave." Penalty: 12 penalty units. A flat negative.
GIVEN `the work is for hire or reward` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is in the hours of my leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35 -- I may do the work` `the work is for hire or reward` `it is in the hours of my leave` MEANS
    IF `the work is for hire or reward` AND `it is in the hours of my leave`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 35 forbids only work for hire or reward in the hours of the leave)

-- s 37(2) "An employer must keep a long service leave record relating to an employee during the employee's period of
-- continuous employment by the employer." (3) "... for at least 7 years after the employee stops working for the
-- employer." After the 7 years the Act is silent (NOTHING).
GIVEN `I still work there` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day I stopped working there` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(2), (3) -- my employer must still keep my record` `I still work there` `the day I stopped working there` `today` MEANS
    IF `I still work there`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the day` `today` `is on or before` (`the same day` 7 `years after` `the day I stopped working there`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: "at least 7 years" sets a minimum; after it the Act says nothing)

-- s 37(6) "An employer must not refuse a request by an employee (or an employee's personal representative) to provide the
-- employee (or the personal representative) with a copy of a long service leave record relating to the employee." No
-- request: the duty has not arisen (NOTHING, fork F14).
GIVEN `I have asked for a copy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(6) -- my employer must give me a copy of my record` `I have asked for a copy` MEANS
    IF `I have asked for a copy`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: the duty arises on a request)

§§ `Parts 4 to 6 -- superior and accrued entitlements, disclosure (ss 46 to 50)`

-- s 47(1) "If, immediately before 27 March 2006, an award provided a long service leave entitlement that was more
-- beneficial to an employee in any respect than the entitlement provided in Part 5 of the Long Service Leave Act 1992, the
-- employee is entitled under this Act to that superior entitlement instead of the employee's relevant entitlement under
-- this Act." (2) "... whether or not the employee was employed immediately before 27 March 2006." s 46 "award ... in
-- relation to an employee and the employee's employer, means an award -- (i) that was binding on the employer immediately
-- before 27 March 2006 or would have been ...; and (ii) to which the employee's employment was subject ... or would have
-- been ...".
GIVEN `an award applied to my employer and my employment before 27 March 2006` IS A BOOLEAN, `it was more beneficial in any respect than Part 5 of the 1992 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47 -- I am entitled to the superior award entitlement` `an award applied to my employer and my employment before 27 March 2006` `it was more beneficial in any respect than Part 5 of the 1992 Act` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`an award applied to my employer and my employment before 27 March 2006` AND `it was more beneficial in any respect than Part 5 of the 1992 Act`)

-- s 48 "protected accrued long service leave entitlement ... means an entitlement to long service leave -- (a) that accrued
-- by operation of an award that has subsequently been varied, set aside, ceased to have effect or was revoked under Part 10
-- of the Workplace Relations Act 1996 ...; or (b) ... an award that is no longer applicable ... under Division 5 of Part 11
-- ...; or (c) ... an employment agreement that has subsequently been terminated under [Division 9 of Part 8, or s 170MH] ...;
-- or (d) ... an agreement that is no longer applicable ... under Division 3 or 4 of Part 11 ...". s 49 "An employee who is
-- or was at any time entitled to a protected accrued long service leave entitlement is entitled to the benefit of that
-- entitlement under this Act regardless of the status of the award or agreement ...". A "means" definition.
GIVEN `it accrued under an award or agreement that ended or stopped applying in one of the s 48 ways` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 -- I keep my protected accrued entitlement` `it accrued under an award or agreement that ended or stopped applying in one of the s 48 ways` MEANS
    `yes or no` `it accrued under an award or agreement that ended or stopped applying in one of the s 48 ways`

-- s 50(1) "At least 7 days before entering into an employment agreement that would modify or remove an employee's
-- entitlements under this Act, the employer must notify the employee in writing of the modification or removal". (2) "...
-- the notice must state whether the proposed agreement modifies or removes ... (a) an entitlement to long service leave on
-- completing 7 years of continuous service; (b) any entitlement arising from the operation of section 47 or 49." Notice on
-- a day at least 7 days before the day of the agreement (the notice day plus 7 on or before the agreement day; fork F15).
GIVEN `the agreement modifies or removes my entitlements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was notified in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice stated what was modified or removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE
      `the day of the agreement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50 -- I was notified in time` `the agreement modifies or removes my entitlements` `I was notified in writing` `the notice stated what was modified or removed` `the day of the notice` `the day of the agreement` MEANS
    IF NOT `the agreement modifies or removes my entitlements`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 50 speaks only of agreements that modify or remove entitlements)
    ELSE `yes or no` (    `I was notified in writing`
                      AND `the notice stated what was modified or removed`
                      AND `the day` (`the date` 7 `days after` `the day of the notice`) `is on or before` `the day of the agreement`)
